# Dealality additive development & non-regression (permanent)

Applies to **all** Dealality streams: GDI, ADP, Hotel Explorer, Brand Explorer, Deal Opportunities, Operator Explorer, Census/HI, Integration.

## Doctrine

New functionality must be **additive** and must **not silently regress** previously accepted UI layouts, opportunity inventory, data accessibility, or customer-facing functionality.

An enhancement is complete only when the new capability works **and** previously accepted functionality continues to work.

## Required before certification

1. Establish the pre-change baseline for affected surfaces.
2. Compare UI and workflows after the change.
3. Compare inventories using **actual record IDs**, not counts alone.
4. Classify differences as intentional vs unintended.
5. Resolve unintended regressions before claiming done.
6. Include a non-regression assessment in the PR closeout.
7. Add automated regression coverage when a defect class is identified.

## Integration Controller

Must **block acceptance** on unintentional regression of previously approved functionality, data accessibility, or presentation.

Intentional redesign/removal/material change requires **explicit founder approval**.

## Do not

- Redesign existing components unless explicitly requested.
- Silently hide, overwrite, or downgrade accepted intelligence.
- Bypass publication/authorization gates to force KPI or inventory parity.
- Spin up a separate infrastructure project solely for this principle — incorporate into existing workflows.

